---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';
import wineries from '../../data/wineries.json';

const topRated = [...wineries].sort((a, b) => (b.rating || 0) - (a.rating || 0)).slice(0, 10);
const petFriendlyTop = [...wineries]
  .filter((w) => w.pet_friendly)
  .sort((a, b) => (b.rating || 0) - (a.rating || 0))
  .slice(0, 6);
const familyTop = [...wineries]
  .filter((w) => w.kid_friendly?.allowed)
  .sort((a, b) => (b.rating || 0) - (a.rating || 0))
  .slice(0, 6);

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'Best Temecula Wineries (2026 Guide)',
  description:
    'Independent guide to the best Temecula wineries — top-rated estates, first-visit picks, pet-friendly options, and how to choose from the full Temecula wineries list.',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Bellie Acres Wine' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Bellie Acres Wine', url: 'https://bellieacreswine.com/' },
  mainEntityOfPage: 'https://bellieacreswine.com/guides/best-temecula-wineries/',
  dateModified: '2026-07-27',
};
---

<Layout
  title="Best Temecula Wineries (2026 Guide)"
  description="Best Temecula wineries guide — top-rated Temecula Valley estates, first-visit picks, pet-friendly options, and how to choose from our full Temecula wineries directory and list."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <Navbar />

  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-14">
    <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[2px] text-[var(--accent)] font-medium mb-3">
      <a href="/guides" class="hover:underline">Guides</a> · Updated July 2026
    </p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl font-serif tracking-tight leading-tight">
      Best Temecula Wineries
    </h1>
    <p class="text-xl text-stone-600 mt-5 leading-relaxed">
      There isn’t one universal “best Temecula winery” — the right stop depends on sparkling vs. bold reds, patio energy, kids, dogs, and how many pours you want in a day.
      This guide uses ratings and practical filters from our independent
      <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/wineries">Temecula wineries directory</a>
      so you can shortlist faster.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/wineries" class="px-5 py-2.5 rounded-full bg-[var(--primary)] text-white text-sm font-medium hover:opacity-90">Full wineries list</a>
      <a href="/guides/first-timer-tasting-route" class="px-5 py-2.5 rounded-full border border-stone-300 text-sm font-medium hover:border-[var(--accent)]">First-timer route</a>
      <a href="/map" class="px-5 py-2.5 rounded-full border border-stone-300 text-sm font-medium hover:border-[var(--accent)]">Wine map</a>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-14 prose-none">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl tracking-tight mb-4">How we define “best”</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
        For this Temecula wine guide, “best” means a strong visitor fit: solid community ratings in our directory data,
        clear tasting identity, and trip logistics you can plan around. Featured listings are paid placements on the site —
        they help discovery, but this best-of ranking is sorted by rating so you can compare fairly.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-5 space-y-2 text-stone-700 list-disc pl-6">
        <li>Start with top-rated estates if you want crowd favorites.</li>
        <li>Filter for pets or families when that changes the day.</li>
        <li>Confirm hours, fees, and reservations on the winery’s official site before you drive.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl tracking-tight mb-3">Top-rated Temecula wineries right now</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-600 mb-8">
        Highest ratings from our current Temecula wineries list ({wineries.length} estates). Ratings are directory snapshots — always re-check recent visitor notes and the estate website.
      </p>
      <ol class="space-y-4">
        {topRated.map((w, i) => (
          <li class="rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5 sm:p-6 flex gap-4 items-start">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[var(--primary)] text-white flex items-center justify-center font-semibold shrink-0">
              {i + 1}
            </div>
            <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
              <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
                <a href={`/wineries/${w.slug}`} class="font-serif text-2xl text-stone-900 hover:text-[var(--accent)]">
                  {w.name}
                </a>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-stone-800">{w.rating} / 5</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-stone-600 mt-1 text-sm">
                {w.location} · {w.price_range}
                {w.varietals?.[0] ? ` · Known for ${w.varietals[0]}` : ''}
              </p>
              <p class="text-stone-700 mt-3 leading-relaxed line-clamp-3">{w.description}</p>
              <a href={`/wineries/${w.slug}`} class="inline-block mt-3 text-[var(--accent)] font-medium hover:underline">
                View directory listing →
              </a>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl tracking-tight mb-4">Strong pet-friendly picks</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-3">
          {petFriendlyTop.map((w) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`/wineries/${w.slug}`} class="font-medium text-stone-900 hover:text-[var(--accent)]">
                {w.name}
              </a>
              <span class="text-stone-500 text-sm"> · {w.rating}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <a href="/guides/pet-friendly-wineries" class="inline-block mt-4 text-[var(--accent)] font-medium hover:underline">
          Full pet-friendly guide →
        </a>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl tracking-tight mb-4">Family-friendlier options</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-3">
          {familyTop.map((w) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`/wineries/${w.slug}`} class="font-medium text-stone-900 hover:text-[var(--accent)]">
                {w.name}
              </a>
              <span class="text-stone-500 text-sm"> · {w.rating}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mt-4">Policies vary by time of day — confirm on site.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 space-y-5">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl tracking-tight">Match “best” to the actual day you are booking</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
        A first-timer who wants one memorable patio and a sit-down lunch should not copy a collector’s four-stop red
        crawl. Couples celebrating often want sparkling first, a view table, and time — not a ranked list of ten names.
        Families need shorter windows and clearer policies. Dog owners need outdoor shade. Heat-sensitive guests need
        morning seats. “Best Temecula wineries” is a planning filter, not a trophy case.
      </p>
      <p class="text-lg text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
        Use this page to circle two or three estates that share a corridor. Then open the
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/map">wine map</a> and our
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/guides/how-many-wineries-one-day">how many wineries in one day</a>
        guide so the shortlist survives contact with parking lots. If you only have a half day, one excellent stop plus
        a real meal beats three compressed flights. If you have a full Saturday, two clustered tastings and lunch still
        beat five pins you cannot actually reach without rushing.
      </p>
      <p class="text-lg text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
        Ratings in our list are snapshots, not lab scores. A 4.8 estate can feel wrong if the patio is fully booked, the
        live music is loud, or the pour list that day is all heavy reds when you wanted sparkling. Always read the
        estate’s current tasting menu. Confirm fees. Screenshot the reservation. Leave white space. That operational
        seriousness is how “best of” lists become good days.
      </p>
      <p class="text-lg text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
        Independent editorial ranking is never paid Featured placement. Featured helps discovery on the list page; this
        guide sorts by rating so you can compare fairly. Smaller estates missing from the top ten can still be the best
        Temecula winery for your palate — especially if you care about a specific varietal, a quiet weekday conversation,
        or a hillside view. Browse the full list after you finish this shortlist.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl tracking-tight mb-4">Build a day around the best stops</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
        Once you’ve circled two or three favorites from this best Temecula wineries shortlist, open the
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/map">Temecula wine map</a> and our
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/guides/first-timer-tasting-route">first-timer tasting route</a>
        so drive time doesn’t eat the afternoon. For food after pours, browse
        <a class="text-[var(--accent)] underline" href="/pairings">Temecula wine pairing ideas</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl tracking-tight">How to use the top-ten list without becoming a tourist cliché</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
        Circle two names that share a road. Ignore the rest until those two are booked. If both are slammed, drop to
        the next rating on the same corridor instead of leaping to a distant famous name. Geography is part of quality.
        A slightly lower rating next door will beat a perfect score across a thirty-minute transfer when you only have
        an afternoon.
      </p>
      <p class="text-lg text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
        Read each profile for atmosphere: resort energy versus boutique conversation, patio versus formal room, sparkling
        versus reds. Then confirm today’s menu. The ranking cannot see a private event, a heat wave, or a sold-out view
        deck. You can. That last check is the difference between a best-of list and a best day.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl tracking-tight">First visit versus return visit</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
        First visits should optimize for welcome, food access, and a corridor you can learn. Return visits can chase a
        specific Syrah, a quieter boutique, or a view you skipped. Do not copy a collector’s third-trip list on your
        first Saturday. Learn the valley, then specialize. The top-rated names are a doorway, not a lifetime assignment.
      </p>
      <p class="text-lg text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
        When friends ask for “the best winery,” answer with a question: sparkling or reds, kids or quiet, weekend or
        Thursday, view or conversation. Then send them this page plus the map. That is more honest than a single trophy
        name, and it is how independent guides stay useful after the ranking screenshot fades.
      </p>
    </section>

      <section class="mt-10 space-y-4">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl tracking-tight font-serif text-stone-900">Keep the shortlist short</h2>
      <p>
        Independent travel guidance from Bellie Acres Wine stays practical on purpose: clustered drives, reserved seats,
        honest heat, real meals, and a designated driver. Confirm every fee, pour list, and outdoor policy with the
        estate before you leave the hotel. Harvest weeks, holiday weekends, and sold-out terraces change the product
        without changing the grapes. Plan the day you can actually keep, then enjoy the valley instead of managing a
        spreadsheet of leftover pins.
      </p>
      </section>

    <section class="mt-14 rounded-3xl bg-stone-100 border border-stone-200 p-8">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl mb-3">Want the complete directory?</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
        This guide highlights standouts. The full <strong>Temecula wine directory</strong> and searchable
        <strong> Temecula wineries list</strong> live on one page — including smaller estates that may be the best Temecula winery <em>for your</em> taste.
      </p>
      <a
        href="/wineries"
        class="inline-flex mt-6 px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-[var(--primary)] text-white font-medium hover:opacity-90"
      >
        Open full wineries list →
      </a>
    </section>

    <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mt-12 leading-relaxed">
      Independent editorial guide for adults 21+. Bellie Acres Wine does not sell alcohol. Hours, fees, pet rules, and availability change — verify directly with each Temecula winery.
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>
